@domain:findings @area:suppression @from:gandalf/fingerprint
Feature: Recognising accepted findings in a baseline
  Teams that commit a .gandalf-baseline.json rely on gandalf recognising each accepted finding on every later run and every later gandalf version, so only genuinely new findings are reported.

  Background:
    Given the repository has a committed .gandalf-baseline.json listing the findings the team accepted

  @id:findings.suppression.001 @rule:findings.baseline.accepted-finding-survives-line-moves @verified @source:src/gandalf/fingerprint.py#fingerprint_keys @test:tests/test_findings.py#test_fingerprint_still_line_insensitive @test:tests/test_suppress.py#test_fingerprint_line_insensitive
  Scenario Outline: An accepted finding stays accepted when it moves to another line
    Given the baseline accepts the ruff finding E501 "line too long" in src/a.py reported at line <old_line>
    When the operator runs gandalf after code above it was edited so the same finding is now reported at line <new_line>
    Then the finding is counted as suppressed
    And the ruff gate does not report it among its remaining findings

    Examples:
      | old_line | new_line |
      | 1        | 99       |
      | 12       | 40       |

  @id:findings.suppression.002 @rule:findings.baseline.changed-message-is-a-new-finding @verified @source:src/gandalf/fingerprint.py#fingerprint_keys @test:tests/test_suppress.py#test_fingerprint_line_insensitive
  Scenario: A finding whose message changed is no longer covered by the baseline
    Given the baseline accepts the ruff finding E501 with message "x" in a.py
    When the operator runs gandalf and ruff now reports E501 in a.py with message "y"
    Then the finding is reported as a remaining finding of the ruff gate
    And it is not counted as suppressed

  @id:findings.suppression.003 @rule:findings.baseline.survives-gandalf-upgrades @verified @source:src/gandalf/fingerprint.py#fingerprint_keys @test:tests/test_findings.py#test_fingerprint_is_stable_for_known_findings @test:tests/test_findings.py#test_fingerprint_vocabulary_is_frozen
  Scenario Outline: A baseline written by an earlier gandalf keeps accepting the same findings after an upgrade
    Given the baseline was generated by an earlier gandalf version and accepts the <gate> finding <rule> in <path>
    And the tool still reports that finding unchanged
    When the operator runs the upgraded gandalf
    Then the finding is counted as suppressed
    And its baseline fingerprint is <fingerprint>

    Examples:
      | gate    | rule       | path       | fingerprint                              |
      | ruff    | E501       | src/a.py   | 7b959079a6b363f06dd56522357092823810133f |
      | bandit  | B105       | src/c.py   | e18dc25e2f9d074cc726c914f925f3db3432da56 |
      | semgrep | py.lang.x  | src/b.py   | 1f95489d888b00dbcf02041e0eff8383dc40b548 |
      | trivy   | CVE-2021-1 | alpine:3.1 | c4f79753892ee22c50032f9c77cdee3a33fe6cc3 |

  @id:findings.suppression.004 @rule:findings.baseline.target-less-findings-accepted-everywhere @verified @source:src/gandalf/fingerprint.py#fingerprint_keys @test:tests/test_findings.py#test_fingerprint_vocabulary_is_frozen @questionable
  Scenario: Accepting a vulnerability found in one container image accepts it in every image
    Given the baseline accepts the trivy finding CVE-2021-1 "boom" reported for target alpine:3.1
    When the operator runs gandalf and trivy reports CVE-2021-1 "boom" for target debian:12
    Then the debian:12 finding is counted as suppressed
    And the trivy gate does not report it among its remaining findings
